'''Game Boy Advance Video''' is a series of [[Game Boy Advance]] cartridges that contain episodes of a cartoon or a movie that can be viewed on a Game Boy Advance. The first Game Boy Advance Video cartridges were released in 2004.

With the exception of the Pokémon releases, they were developed and published by {{wp|Majesco Entertainment}}. The Pokémon releases were published by [[Nintendo]]. They were released in North America and Australia<!--Not that they weren't released in the UK, just that it hasn't been confirmed-->. In the United States, the {{wp|MSRP}} was US$19.99.<ref name="Pokémon GBA Video">[https://web.archive.org/web/20090206231212/http://www.gba-video.com/pokemon.html Pokémon GBA Video | Game Boy Advance Video]</ref>

The cartridges were intentionally made incompatible with the [[Game Boy Player]] so that users could not record the shows to media such as blank VHS tapes or DVDs.<ref>[https://web.archive.org/web/20161003070357/http://www.nintendo.com/consumer/systems/gameboyadvance/agb_video_faq.jsp Nintendo | Game Boy Advance Video FAQ]</ref>

The first cartridges were released in May 2004 in North America and contained episodes from {{wp|Nickelodeon}} shows.<ref>[https://web.archive.org/web/20150131193956/http://www.gba-video.com/pressrelease2.html Game Boy Advance Video - Majesco Ships first "Game Boy Advance Video" Titles]</ref> In June 2004, the first two volumes of {{aniseries|PTS}} were released in North America. Later releases included {{wp|Disney Channel}} shows, other anime such as ''{{wp|Dragon Ball GT}}'' and ''{{wp|Yu-Gi-Oh! Duel Monsters|Yu-Gi-Oh!}}'', and the {{wp|DreamWorks Animation|DreamWorks}} films ''{{wp|Shrek}}'', ''{{wp|Shrek 2}}'' and ''{{wp|Shark Tale}}''.

